# Rust / Cargo
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Cargo.lock IS committed — this workspace ships binaries (chapr-coord,
# chapr-endpoint), so the lockfile is tracked for reproducible builds
# (Rust guidance for applications).

# Coordinator runtime artifacts (in case coord is run with default paths in-repo).
chapr-blobs/
*.db
*.db-*

# MCPB bundle staging + packed deliverable. build-mcpb.ps1 defaults to
# -OutDir ./build and copies target/release/chapr-endpoint.exe into it.
build/
*.mcpb

# Release staging. The release workflow assembles named artifacts here before
# uploading them to a GitHub Release; the artifacts themselves never live in git.
# (A customer DEPLOYABLE repo does commit its binaries — this one does not.)
dist/

# Scratch working dir.
scratchpad/

# Local editor/OS cruft.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.log

# --- Internal development tooling — kept LOCAL, never published. -------------
# The code is the product; these are private working docs / agent tooling.
# (gitignore does not delete them — they remain on disk for local use.)
#
# `LOGBOOK.md` and `CLAUDE.md` were committed on 2026-08-14 on the explicit
# grounds that "the repo is private, so there was never a disclosure argument."
# That premise expired when the project went Apache-2.0 and public (D-033), so
# the decision is reversed here and they are untracked again.
#
# What they are: ~200 KB of candid internal reasoning — every decision and its
# rationale, issue histories, the customer deployable by name, a collaborator's
# plugin internals, share paths. None of it is secret; all of it is written for
# an internal audience and not for the world. What a public reader actually
# needs from them belongs in README.md, restated deliberately.
#
# NOTE: they were also purged from git history (filter-branch, 2026-08-20), not
# merely untracked, because a public clone would otherwise still yield them via
# `git show`. Do not re-add them: the purge cost a force-push and cannot be
# repeated cheaply.
#
# NOTE: the 2026-08-14 backup argument was real and is now live again — the
# logbook is irreplaceable project memory sitting on one laptop. It needs a home
# in a private repo.
#
# NOTE (2026-08-21) — REVERSED for the logbook, by jok: "add the logs to the repo,
# they belong there for open source -> open project." `LOGBOOK.md` and `logbook/`
# are now TRACKED. Everything above about them stands as history, not as policy.
#
# What made that safe rather than just decided: the customer-identifying strings
# were scrubbed first — the deployable repo, the collaborator's plugin, its scripts
# and its Danish folder names are now described by role instead of named. The
# engineering reasoning never depended on the names. Named *people* stay: they are
# this project's own contributors, listed in NOTICE.
#
# What is deliberately still public-by-choice inside it: open issue narratives with
# exact file:line locations, including unfixed ones. That is consistent with
# docs/security.md, which already says there is no embargo process because
# pretending otherwise would be theatre.
#
# `CLAUDE.md` stays untracked — it is agent instructions, not project memory, and
# nobody asked for it. That is a separate call if it ever comes up.
# NOTE (2026-08-21): `specs/` consolidates everything that is jok's *working
# material* rather than documentation — the original architecture/implementation
# specs, the 0.2→0.5 plan and its review, design inspiration, scratch HTML. It
# replaces the per-file rules that used to list `docs/init spec/` and
# `docs/status.html`.
#
# The dividing line, and the reason `docs/` is now short: **`docs/` holds what a
# reader needs; `specs/` holds what development ran on.** A whole DIRECTORY again,
# for D-036's reason — a scratch file added later cannot slip into the public repo
# by nobody remembering to add a line.
#
# Known consequence, unchanged by the move: the code cites ~30 `§n` anchors that
# point into `specs/fmcp-architecture-concept.md`, so those references do not
# resolve for a public reader. Publishing that one spec is roadmap item 2.3's
# remaining half — it is language-agnostic architecture, not customer material.
.claude/
specs/
CLAUDE.md
